      "@id": "#claim",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "name": "Entry 23: move-grid connectivity bias in simujaules terrain-mode optimal energy",
      "text": "Yes — and terrain roughly doubles the pure-geometry prediction: sq8 sits +12.7% median (+47% p90) above a converged near-continuum reference on the deployed 5 m DTM; the mechanism is height oscillation under the asymmetric climb/descent cost, not octile distance. Profile-integrated sq16 recovers ≈⅔ of the bias; NAIVE long-edge costing flips the error's sign (the trap: it flattens the relief it crosses). Pre-registration scorecard against the shipped worker: wall-time confirmed, field-median borderline, budget-reach miscalibrated — pre-register distributions, not point ranges.",
